Applied by tools/build_hactool.py to SciresM/hactool (ISC) at 1d64a83450e025622f3468c28fc4164dad2c5ef6, ours.
The x86-64 multiply-accumulate asm of hactool's bundled mbedtls 2.6.1 (MULADDC in bn_mul.h) adds into memory through
rdi and changes the flags without saying so. gcc happens to keep that code correct; clang (the Linux release's
toolchain) keeps memory values in registers across it at -O1 and above, the RSA arithmetic goes wrong, and every
signature check fails (NCA header, NPDM, ACID), which stops the merge of the update. Later mbedtls releases name the
same two clobbers.

diff --git a/mbedtls/include/mbedtls/bn_mul.h b/mbedtls/include/mbedtls/bn_mul.h
index cac3f14..c787b0a 100644
--- a/mbedtls/include/mbedtls/bn_mul.h
+++ b/mbedtls/include/mbedtls/bn_mul.h
@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@
 #define MULADDC_STOP                        \
         : "+c" (c), "+D" (d), "+S" (s)      \
         : "b" (b)                           \
-        : "rax", "rdx", "r8"                \
+        : "rax", "rdx", "r8", "memory", "cc" \
     );
 
 #endif /* AMD64 */
